// IR migration: selector rule generation was removed.
// XFAIL: *
// A behavior that writes a fixed register besides its value output roots no
// selection rule: the tile would drop the second write and bind the fixed
// read as a free operand (a `pop` matching any load). A fixed-register read
// alone stays legal — it surfaces as a demand.

// RUN: tmdlc --action=emit-rust --dialect=test --output=- %S/../Inputs/fixed-write-rules.tmdl | filecheck %s

// CHECK: static RULE_LOADFIXEDBASE
// CHECK-NOT: static RULE_POPLIKE
// CHECK-NOT: static RULE_PUSHLIKE
